# Line endings in this repo follow one rule, and it is about who reads the file.
#
#   DOCUMENTS ARE LF.  Markdown, and anything else only humans and modern tools
#   read. There is no reason for a doc to carry CRLF and it makes noisy diffs.
#
#   DOS FILES ARE CRLF, BYTE FOR BYTE.  Anything a 1990s DOS tool reads or IS --
#   .PAS, .ASM, .INC, .BAT, .CFG, and the binaries. This is a reconstruction
#   project measured by byte comparison against 1994 executables, so git must
#   never rewrite a single byte of them.
#
# `core.autocrlf` is false here, so before this file existed git simply stored
# whatever was on disk and the rule was a habit rather than a guarantee.

# default: leave every byte alone
* -text

# documents: normalise to LF on the way in, check out LF everywhere
*.md    text eol=lf

# DOS sources and configs: never converted, but worth diffing
*.PAS   -text diff
*.pas   -text diff
*.ASM   -text diff
*.asm   -text diff
*.INC   -text diff
*.inc   -text diff
*.BAT   -text diff
*.bat   -text diff
*.CFG   -text diff
*.conf  -text diff
*.py    -text diff

# genuinely binary: never try
*.EXE   binary
*.exe   binary
*.TPU   binary
*.OBJ   binary
*.DAT   binary
*.dat   binary
*.bin   binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
